+- **Part A, underline** (`src/list_model.rs` `match_range`, `ListModel::row_match`; `src/tui.rs` `row_line`).
+  While the filter is non-empty, the first case-insensitive occurrence of it in the alias, and in the host when
+  the row shows it (50 columns or more), is drawn with the underline attribute; nothing else in a row is. The
+  search uses the filter's own rule (`str::to_lowercase` on both sides) and maps the hit back to whole
+  characters of the original string through per-character lowercase lengths, so it stays exact where lowercasing
+  changes the length. Underline is an attribute, so it is drawn under `NO_COLOR`; crossterm still writes no
+  colour SGR then.
+- **Part B, help overlay** (`HELP_LINES`, `ListModel::help_open`; `src/tui.rs` `render_help`). `?` outside
+  filter mode opens it; `?` or `Esc` closes it (Esc does not touch the filter); every other key except Ctrl-C is
+  ignored while it is open. It replaces the whole screen, one help line per row with a one-space indent, so no
+  list text shares a row with it; small terminals clip it. In filter mode `?` is filter text.
+- **Part C, selection** (`ListModel::refilter`, `ListModel::scroll`). After an edit the previously selected
+  destination stays selected if it is still shown (found by binary search in the ascending `shown` list),
+  otherwise the first shown row is selected. The model now owns the list window: `scroll(height)` keeps the
+  previous window position, clamps it so the window is always full when enough rows match, and moves it only as
+  far as needed to keep the selection visible. When the selection is kept, it keeps its screen row where
+  possible. Ratatui's own offset logic does not back-fill a window that a shrinking list leaves short, so the
+  offset is set explicitly.
